# The five tools the AppImage bundler of tauri-bundler 2.9.4 (the one
# inside @tauri-apps/cli 2.11.5, see package-lock.json) downloads into
# ~/.cache/tauri when it builds the AppImage, as they were on 2026-09-05,
# except linuxdeploy-plugin-appimage, taken from a tagged release on
# 2026-10-16.
#
# The bundler fetches them from references that move (release assets that
# can be re-uploaded, a `master` branch, a `continuous` release), verifies
# nothing, runs three of them on the build machine and ships AppRun and
# the gtk hook inside the AppImage itself. Tauri once vendored the scripts
# (PR #14390) and went back to downloading them (PR #14841). The bundler
# skips a download when the file already sits in its cache, so
# reproducible/targets/linux.sh downloads the five files itself, checks them
# against this list and only then starts the build. The check must come
# first: once the bundler has linuxdeploy it overwrites three bytes at
# offset 8, to hide the file from AppImage integration tools.
#
# Sources, in the order the bundler names them
# (crates/tauri-bundler/src/bundle/linux/appimage/linuxdeploy.rs, tag
# tauri-cli-v2.11.5 of tauri-apps/tauri):
#   AppRun-x86_64                         https://github.com/tauri-apps/binary-releases/releases/download/apprun-old/AppRun-x86_64
#   linuxdeploy-x86_64.AppImage           https://github.com/tauri-apps/binary-releases/releases/download/linuxdeploy/linuxdeploy-x86_64.AppImage
#   linuxdeploy-plugin-gtk.sh             https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tauri-apps/linuxdeploy-plugin-gtk/master/linuxdeploy-plugin-gtk.sh
#   linuxdeploy-plugin-gstreamer.sh       https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tauri-apps/linuxdeploy-plugin-gstreamer/master/linuxdeploy-plugin-gstreamer.sh
#   linuxdeploy-plugin-appimage.AppImage  https://github.com/linuxdeploy/linuxdeploy-plugin-appimage/releases/download/continuous/linuxdeploy-plugin-appimage-x86_64.AppImage
#
# The two scripts are fetched from the commit that holds the bytes below,
# not from `master`, which has moved since these hashes were taken:
#   linuxdeploy-plugin-gtk.sh        tauri-apps/linuxdeploy-plugin-gtk b5eb8d05b4c0ed40107fe2158c5d8527f94568ef
#   linuxdeploy-plugin-gstreamer.sh  tauri-apps/linuxdeploy-plugin-gstreamer 2a2e67491c32995a3f279ad0ecbe77abd512b42a
#
# The `continuous` release of linuxdeploy-plugin-appimage is rebuilt on
# the 1st of every month, so its hash changes even when the source does
# not. The plugin is fetched from the release 1-alpha-20250213-1 instead
# (commit a96502d15ce19ec1df3d46e6cbe87ddf38589a71), whose file stays.
# GitHub publishes no digest for it and the upstream run that built it
# has aged out. Its provenance: uploaded by github-actions[bot] on
# 2025-02-13 and never replaced since (asset 228937581), and the same
# hash pinned the next day by KDE Craft (craft-blueprints-kde
# cebd8e789). Its source differs from the `continuous` build pinned
# before (536b068) only in build flags; it bundles appimagetool build
# 227 instead of 295, with the same mksquashfs 4.6.1.
#
# When @tauri-apps/cli moves, read that file again at the matching tag:
# if a URL or a file name changed, update release.yml and this list. To
# refresh a hash on purpose, download the file, compare it with the
# previous one (a script diff is readable; a new binary should come with
# a reason), then run `sha256sum` on the five files in the cache
# directory and paste its output below.
f30140a43a0a59e46db21bdefdf749b9e9f2c6946e92afabbacf98b8ae73fb4f  AppRun-x86_64
e762bea85c8eb0d4b3508d46e5c1f037f717d0f9303ae3b4aafc8b04991fa1ef  linuxdeploy-x86_64.AppImage
cb379f9b0733e9ad9f8bd78f8c2fa038aef2478523bb7d4c8e64ff6a1ea3501a  linuxdeploy-plugin-gtk.sh
c107b49d84edbffc6ab226ed1007e0626a4f7aa2c3a36b7782bef62351d49e94  linuxdeploy-plugin-gstreamer.sh
992d502a248e14ab185448ddf6f6e7d25558cb84d4623c354c3af350c25fccb3  linuxdeploy-plugin-appimage.AppImage
